{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097918-undertale-like-chronicle","id":1097918,"title":"Undertale-Like Chronicle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T17:44:55-07:00","id":1097918,"title":"Undertale-Like Chronicle?","content":"Undertale is partially based on the monsters not being really evil for the most part, but the monsters in CoD are often evil by necessity or opportunity. I'm not sure what the power of Determination would be in CoD either.<br /> <br /> Besides conveying the themes of Undertale, how would one adapt the setting? An all-out war between humans and supernaturals is probably too much. Would something smaller in scope work?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could just borrow the themes without using the Underground. The players could be a special Cell of Hunters who are not interested in killing the monsters, but learning about them and helping create a world where they can coexist with humans (if the players want to go Pacifist, that is). Possibly a Network Zero and liberal Union focused Chronicle, with the antagonists being opportunistic monsters who want to take advantage of these well-intentioned Hunters, and more traditional Hunters who do not want an Unveiled Masquerade. And who says the Big Revelation about supernaturals to the world would be the end of the game? You could build more story arcs around the ensuing fallout. In fact, the &quot;World Of Darkness Revealed&quot; Shard from page 136 of Mirrors could serve as inspiration for this.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?<br /> <br /> EDIT: It would also be a good idea to let the players have some dots in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813925-dialling-my-brain-back-down-true-friendship\"><b>Soulmate Supernatural Style</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:48:32-07:00","id":1097963,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Monsters are a more benign relative of the Horrors of Beasts?<br /> <br /> I haven't played terribgly far into Undertale, but from what little I've seen, I could also see arguments for the underground world being the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T21:27:08-07:00","id":1097976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097918-undertale-like-chronicle?p=1097963#post1097963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__doub