Lost, in which case Sans is Unseemly and Asriel/Flowey is a Loyalist.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-29-2017, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T22:11:20-07:00","id":1097984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097918-undertale-like-chronicle?p=1097976#post1097976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's definitely the Hedge, in my opinion. That interpretation only gets stronger the further you get in the story.<br /> <br /> I imagine everyone who has an interest in avoiding spoilers has played through at least the main three paths by now, but spoiler tagging this just in case...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Under David's Seeming paradigm, Frisk is a Fairest, Chara is a Darkling, and the player is both of their Keeper. I could also see an argument for all of the monsters being Lost who couldn't escape (until the True Pacifist ending). I could <i>also</i> see an argument for the characters with knowledge of saving being the only Lost, in which case Sans is Unseemly and Asgore/Flowey is a Loyalist.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to run this Chronicle, it probably wouldn't be straight up the Underground from the game. The whole idea of Saving/Determination would either be gone or reimagined as something else (perhaps a blessing from the Principle). I want a more thematic adaptation rather than a 1 for 1 conversion of everything in the game. That's why I picked a &quot;well meaning Hunters want to help the monsters coexist with humans&quot; scenario.<br /> <br /> However, my take on it could totally start with the characters getting lost in the Hedge shortly after becoming Hunters. They'd be welcomed by good changelings and hobgoblins, which would encourage them to help supernaturals like I described after leaving the Hedge. Kinda like how Frisk is said to become a diplomat for monsterkind after the Pacifist Ending among the fans (except that each Hunter gets to be Frisk in their own way). That is if the players want to do a Pacifist story, of course. I would give them full freedom to go No Mercy if they wanted.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-29-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:50:09-07:00","id":1098003,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I got ya. A CofD chronicle that incorporates themes in common with Undertale rather than reproducing Undertale in CofD.<br /> <br /> That said, I do kind of like the idea of an Undertale-inspired template. Determination as a power stat and LOVE as an Integrity stat. Or maybe vice-versa would be better.<br /> <br /> Actually, since you're thinking about Hunter, Determination could turn out to be what separates hunters from ordinary humans - the reason they are able to risk Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:33:21-07:00","id":1098061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097918-undertale-like-chronicle?p=1098003#post1098003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I got ya. A CofD chronicle that incorporates themes in common with Undertale rather than reproducing Undertale in CofD.<br /> <br /> That said, I do kind of like the idea of an Undertale-inspired template. Determination as a power stat and LOVE as an Integrity stat. Or maybe vice-versa would be better.<br /> <br /> Actually, since you're thinking about Hunter, Determination could turn out to be what separates hunters from ordinary humans - the reason they are able to risk Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that LOVE is a Powerstat and Determination is the Integrity equivalent. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Your LOVE starts out low, and while increasing it makes you more powerful, it also comes with serious drawbacks the higher it gets, just like a Powerstat.<br /> <br /> Determination seems like it would be Harmony-like, but would vary faster. High ratings give bonuses to protecting those you care about and fighting for what you believe in, but makes you reckless, restless and overbearing. At low ratings, you do not become apathetic, but more diplomatic, flexible and friendly, at the cost of being more willing to compromise and accept shades of grey. The middle ground would be ideal, but hard to maintain.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Conviction Powerstat from Mirrors is conceptually similar to Determination (they're both about the incredible feats the human spirit can achieve with enough motivation). I think regular mortals have Conviction too, but Hunters have a lot more due to upholding the Vigil. Conviction already does some very cinematic things, especially when combined with the other abilities of the Hunter template, but you can totally upgrade it to have Determination-like effects (or make Determination level abilities be Merits tied to high Conviction and the Soulmate Supernatural Style).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-29-2017, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}